WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.766 --> 00:00:05.033
On their way to the Snowbelle City Gym

2
00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:07.800
and Ash's eighth Kalos Gym badge challenge,

3
00:00:07.866 --> 00:00:11.900
our heroes are visiting a Pokémon Center in the middle of a forest.

4
00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:20.933
Dedenne!

5
00:00:24.333 --> 00:00:25.433
Huh?

6
00:00:26.633 --> 00:00:28.200
They're all doing fine.

7
00:00:29.366 --> 00:00:31.166
Everyone's in perfect health.

8
00:00:31.233 --> 00:00:33.366
Pika, Pi!

9
00:00:33.433 --> 00:00:34.633
Looking good, buddy.

10
00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:35.966
Pika, Pika.

11
00:00:38.533 --> 00:00:41.433
- What do you wanna do after this, Clemont?
- Let's see.

12
00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:44.600
- Why don't we rest a bit more and then go?
- Sounds great.

13
00:00:46.066 --> 00:00:47.733
Well, Eevee? Feel good?

14
00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:48.966
Eevee.

15
00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:00.400
One at a time!

16
00:01:00.466 --> 00:01:01.700
Wait your turn!

17
00:01:01.766 --> 00:01:03.800
You won't get brushed if you act up!

18
00:01:09.233 --> 00:01:11.266
All right, Braixen, you're next.

19
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:14.866
Pancham, Pan.

20
00:01:15.366 --> 00:01:17.266
There, everyone's brushed.

21
00:01:17.333 --> 00:01:18.933
Wonderful. You're looking great.

22
00:01:19.366 --> 00:01:20.200
Huh?

23
00:01:20.666 --> 00:01:23.533
That's right. I need to check for any new videos.

24
00:01:27.266 --> 00:01:29.233
Huh? I wonder what's going on.

25
00:01:32.866 --> 00:01:35.033
Dear performers, bonjour.

26
00:01:35.533 --> 00:01:39.700
To the talented trainers who are rehearsing for their performances,

27
00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:42.200
one and all, I am Pierre, your host.

28
00:01:42.266 --> 00:01:45.366
And I am thrilled to invite you to my dance party.

29
00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:46.900
Huh?

30
00:01:51.966 --> 00:01:55.266
♪ I stand tall 'Cause I know I'm a winner ♪

31
00:01:56.033 --> 00:01:59.200
♪ Knock me down I'll just get up again ♪

32
00:01:59.733 --> 00:02:03.166
♪ You've met your match Yeah, I'm no beginner ♪

33
00:02:03.233 --> 00:02:05.833
♪ Pokémon, Pokémon ♪

34
00:02:06.433 --> 00:02:07.500
♪ Gotta catch 'em all ♪

35
00:02:07.566 --> 00:02:10.733
♪ I stand tall 'Cause I know I'm a winner ♪

36
00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:13.966
♪ Pokémon, Pokémon ♪

37
00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:15.700
♪ Gotta catch 'em all ♪

38
00:02:26.033 --> 00:02:28.566
My party won't be the same without you.

39
00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:30.700
A dance party.

40
00:02:30.766 --> 00:02:33.800
I wanted to give competing performers a break,

41
00:02:33.866 --> 00:02:35.700
and do it in an elegant way.

42
00:02:35.766 --> 00:02:37.933
So, come and enjoy, s'il vous plaît.

43
00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:41.166
-Wow, sounds like fun.

44
00:02:41.233 --> 00:02:45.233
However, in order to attend, I require one thing.

45
00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:48.033
Ah.

46
00:02:48.533 --> 00:02:52.400
All performers and their Pokémon partners are hereby requested

47
00:02:52.466 --> 00:02:54.766
to attend my dance party with a date.

48
00:02:57.233 --> 00:02:59.533
Whoa. So, you need a date, huh?

49
00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:03.966
Elegant. Fun.

50
00:03:04.033 --> 00:03:09.533
Also, Aria, the Kalos Queen, will be in attendance as my honored guest.

51
00:03:10.033 --> 00:03:11.066
She'll be there, too?

52
00:03:11.133 --> 00:03:13.900
Au revoir, until we meet again.

53
00:03:16.133 --> 00:03:18.600
Please, Serena, can we come along?

54
00:03:18.666 --> 00:03:20.033
You're gonna go, right?

55
00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:22.366
Why not?

56
00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:26.133
Eevee, you wanna go?

57
00:03:26.666 --> 00:03:31.066
There are gonna be lots of people there, but it'll be a great experience.

58
00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:36.500
- Pierre said you have to have a date.
- And the Pokémon do, too.

59
00:03:36.566 --> 00:03:38.633
- How about Bunnelby?
- Huh?

60
00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:39.966
Good idea.

61
00:03:40.433 --> 00:03:41.766
Come on out, Bunnelby.

62
00:03:42.433 --> 00:03:43.266
Elby.

63
00:03:43.733 --> 00:03:47.600
Bunnelby, would you like to go to a dance party as Eevee's date?

64
00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:51.266
I'm sure it's going to be a lot of fun.

65
00:03:53.033 --> 00:03:55.800
- Beh.
- Does that mean Clemont will be your date?

66
00:03:56.733 --> 00:03:57.666
My date?

67
00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:00.733
Clemont, will you?

68
00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:03.133
Me? On a date?

69
00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:05.333
-You'll have a blast.

70
00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:07.766
- Pika, Pika.
- I'll do my best.

71
00:04:07.833 --> 00:04:10.400
But do you really think I'm the right person?

72
00:04:10.466 --> 00:04:12.033
You'll be fine.

73
00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:17.000
Eevee, you're such a wonderful dancer.

74
00:04:17.066 --> 00:04:18.100
They'll all love you.

75
00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:19.666
Eevee.

76
00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:26.066
It should be around here somewhere. Huh?

77
00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:36.866
Awesome. Looks like it's gonna be a lot of fun.

78
00:04:36.933 --> 00:04:37.866
Pikachu!

79
00:04:38.333 --> 00:04:40.233
I know. Look at that crowd.

80
00:04:40.733 --> 00:04:42.366
Are you gonna be all right?

81
00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:45.466
Who knows? I'm wondering about that myself.

82
00:04:45.533 --> 00:04:47.533
You'll be fine, Clemont.

83
00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:48.733
Clemont?

84
00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:52.700
- That means Ash isn't your date, right?
- Huh?

85
00:04:53.133 --> 00:04:55.033
- Miette?
- That's me.

86
00:04:55.766 --> 00:04:56.700
Slurpuff.

87
00:04:56.766 --> 00:04:58.100
It's been a while.

88
00:04:58.633 --> 00:04:59.633
Pika!

89
00:05:00.166 --> 00:05:01.933
So, you guys came, too.

90
00:05:02.333 --> 00:05:03.866
You could be my date.

91
00:05:03.933 --> 00:05:07.066
- Wow, talk about perfect timing.
- Huh?

92
00:05:07.133 --> 00:05:10.366
Please, Ash, it would be so nice if you would be my date.

93
00:05:10.433 --> 00:05:12.666
-Sure. No problem.

94
00:05:14.066 --> 00:05:15.066
That's great.

95
00:05:15.133 --> 00:05:16.300
Thanks, Ash.

96
00:05:18.933 --> 00:05:21.166
- Eevee.
- You caught an Eevee?

97
00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:23.000
Eevee.

98
00:05:23.066 --> 00:05:26.500
Yeah. You'll be amazed when you see Eevee perform.

99
00:05:26.566 --> 00:05:28.133
Such a beautiful dancer.

100
00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:30.700
I saw the Pokémon Showcase you were in.

101
00:05:31.133 --> 00:05:33.066
You'll be great rivals for us.

102
00:05:33.133 --> 00:05:36.166
But for right now, let's enjoy the party.

103
00:05:36.233 --> 00:05:38.866
-Pikachu. Pi?

104
00:05:47.333 --> 00:05:48.300
Huh?

105
00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:51.133
Oh! That Miette.

106
00:05:51.666 --> 00:05:54.166
- Eevee?
- Let's get going, too.

107
00:05:54.233 --> 00:05:56.000
Hmm?

108
00:05:56.066 --> 00:05:57.166
Eevee.

109
00:06:01.766 --> 00:06:04.466
Of course the twerps would show their annoying faces.

110
00:06:04.533 --> 00:06:07.300
Which gives us a great chance to catch Pikachu.

111
00:06:07.766 --> 00:06:11.666
With my beauty and class, I'm going to be the belle of the ball.

112
00:06:12.333 --> 00:06:14.533
Why? I've got it all.

113
00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:17.933
I thought catching Pikachu was the name of the game.

114
00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:19.166
Wob!

115
00:06:19.233 --> 00:06:21.600
Of course, James will be my escort.

116
00:06:21.666 --> 00:06:23.666
Uh, oui, mademoiselle.

117
00:06:23.733 --> 00:06:25.233
Huh?

118
00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:32.000
All right, we've got Miette and Ash. Serena and Clemont, as well.

119
00:06:32.633 --> 00:06:36.266
Everything's in order. And you'll also need these cards.

120
00:06:36.966 --> 00:06:38.166
Huh?

121
00:06:38.233 --> 00:06:39.400
Excuse me. What are they?

122
00:06:39.466 --> 00:06:42.466
You'll need that card for a special event later.

123
00:06:42.533 --> 00:06:46.233
We also have outfits that are available to rent. Over there.

124
00:06:56.866 --> 00:06:58.766
Look at all these dresses.

125
00:06:59.366 --> 00:07:00.300
So many.

126
00:07:03.633 --> 00:07:06.533
- Pika.
- I love this one.

127
00:07:06.600 --> 00:07:08.466
This one. This one, too.

128
00:07:09.633 --> 00:07:11.433
Ah. Those, too.

129
00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:13.100
You're gonna try on more?

130
00:07:15.433 --> 00:07:16.300
Aw.

131
00:07:22.333 --> 00:07:23.933
You look so nice.

132
00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:25.866
You look great, too, Bonnie.

133
00:07:25.933 --> 00:07:28.366
Thank you. I love my dress.

134
00:07:33.466 --> 00:07:35.400
- Aha. There you are.
- Huh?

135
00:07:35.900 --> 00:07:38.433
Sorry. It took a while.

136
00:07:39.300 --> 00:07:41.400
Hmm. Fashionable as expected.

137
00:07:42.033 --> 00:07:43.266
You look great, too.

138
00:07:43.333 --> 00:07:45.500
This thing's pinching on my neck.

139
00:07:45.566 --> 00:07:47.866
We're not used to dressing up like this.

140
00:07:48.633 --> 00:07:50.333
Pikachu.

141
00:07:51.366 --> 00:07:53.233
- Slur?
- Huh? Huh?

142
00:08:00.866 --> 00:08:01.900
It's Aria.

143
00:08:02.833 --> 00:08:04.766
Ladies and gentlemen,

144
00:08:04.833 --> 00:08:08.800
thank you all for graciously attending my dance party today.

145
00:08:10.566 --> 00:08:12.500
And now for our special guest.

146
00:08:12.566 --> 00:08:16.033
I'm honored to introduce our Kalos Queen, Aria.

147
00:08:16.433 --> 00:08:18.033
Nice to see you, everyone.

148
00:08:21.133 --> 00:08:22.100
Huh.

149
00:08:23.666 --> 00:08:25.466
Hmm.

150
00:08:28.366 --> 00:08:29.800
Just you wait, girl.

151
00:08:29.866 --> 00:08:33.200
There's only room for one real Kalos Queen and that's me.

152
00:08:55.366 --> 00:08:57.366
- She's wonderful.
- I know.

153
00:08:57.433 --> 00:08:58.366
Huh?

154
00:08:58.433 --> 00:09:01.366
- Aria really is our ideal.
- Huh.

155
00:09:21.333 --> 00:09:24.466
And now the dance floor is open for all of you.

156
00:09:24.833 --> 00:09:26.700
Please, have a wonderful time.

157
00:09:27.166 --> 00:09:28.800
Come on. Let's dance.

158
00:09:28.866 --> 00:09:29.700
Yeah.

159
00:09:30.633 --> 00:09:32.733
- Clemont, shall we dance?
- Why not?

160
00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:34.766
- Bunnelby.
- Eevee.

161
00:09:46.533 --> 00:09:47.700
And one.

162
00:09:47.766 --> 00:09:48.600
Got it.

163
00:09:49.200 --> 00:09:50.566
- And two.
- Right.

164
00:09:51.666 --> 00:09:53.133
- And three.
- Three.

165
00:09:54.700 --> 00:09:55.866
Yay, Clemont!

166
00:09:55.933 --> 00:09:57.066
Looking good.

167
00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:04.233
- Whoops. Sorry.
- Are you okay?

168
00:10:06.433 --> 00:10:07.733
- Sorry. Oh!
- Aah!

169
00:10:12.266 --> 00:10:13.500
Pika, Pi.

170
00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:15.533
Sorry about that.

171
00:10:15.600 --> 00:10:17.933
Wow, Ash, you've got a hard head.

172
00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:19.033
Oh, well.

173
00:10:22.533 --> 00:10:24.066
Hi there. Having fun?

174
00:10:24.133 --> 00:10:25.800
- Eevee.
- Bunnelby.

175
00:10:25.866 --> 00:10:26.766
I'm glad.

176
00:10:31.666 --> 00:10:34.666
Behold my tasteful, elegant moves.

177
00:10:35.366 --> 00:10:38.766
And one, two. One, two. One, two!

178
00:10:39.866 --> 00:10:42.266
- Again. One, two. One, two.
- Wob.

179
00:10:44.833 --> 00:10:46.833
So many performers here.

180
00:10:46.900 --> 00:10:48.733
All aiming to be Kalos Queen.

181
00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:51.066
We'll have to do our best.

182
00:10:52.100 --> 00:10:53.333
Huh?

183
00:10:53.400 --> 00:10:56.533
All right, everyone, form into circles.

184
00:10:57.166 --> 00:10:59.266
It's time to change partners.

185
00:10:59.333 --> 00:11:00.933
Then let's dance.

186
00:11:06.866 --> 00:11:08.700
Alors, music?

187
00:11:09.400 --> 00:11:10.266
And we're off.

188
00:11:18.133 --> 00:11:22.133
I wonder if Eevee's okay dancing with someone other than Bunnelby.

189
00:11:27.300 --> 00:11:28.866
That's wonderful.

190
00:11:29.800 --> 00:11:31.533
Whoa. Uh...

191
00:11:36.100 --> 00:11:38.133
- Dancing's not hard.
- Aria.

192
00:11:38.600 --> 00:11:40.300
It's easy. Just relax.

193
00:11:40.366 --> 00:11:41.333
Okay.

194
00:11:44.333 --> 00:11:47.600
How did I ever get myself stuck in this mess?

195
00:11:48.300 --> 00:11:50.966
You dance so gracefully, mademoiselle.

196
00:11:51.033 --> 00:11:52.400
Thanks so much.

197
00:11:58.566 --> 00:11:59.800
Huh?

198
00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:14.500
Huh?

199
00:12:21.266 --> 00:12:22.166
Huh?

200
00:12:24.266 --> 00:12:25.933
Well, that's it.

201
00:12:26.000 --> 00:12:27.833
So, Serena, did you have a good time?

202
00:12:27.900 --> 00:12:29.900
I guess I did.

203
00:12:29.966 --> 00:12:31.800
Wish I could have danced more.

204
00:12:32.533 --> 00:12:35.300
All right, let us begin today's main event:

205
00:12:35.366 --> 00:12:37.600
our enchanting tag battle.

206
00:12:37.666 --> 00:12:40.300
There are no Pokémon battles in a Pokémon Showcase.

207
00:12:40.833 --> 00:12:43.066
So, consider this a special treat.

208
00:12:43.900 --> 00:12:47.000
All our participants will be chosen at random.

209
00:12:47.066 --> 00:12:50.066
Please raise the card you received at the reception desk

210
00:12:50.133 --> 00:12:51.866
and hold it up to the light.

211
00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:56.800
If a mark appears, then you're one of our lucky participants.

212
00:12:59.400 --> 00:13:01.933
-The battle begins next.

213
00:13:05.133 --> 00:13:07.133
Who's that Pokémon?

214
00:13:11.033 --> 00:13:12.766
It's Furret.

215
00:13:13.333 --> 00:13:14.400
Furret.

216
00:13:20.333 --> 00:13:23.433
It's a battle. That's what I'm talking about.

217
00:13:24.733 --> 00:13:26.266
The pairings are great.

218
00:13:28.733 --> 00:13:31.100
Ash and Serena, go for it!

219
00:13:34.066 --> 00:13:35.566
I win battles, too.

220
00:13:35.633 --> 00:13:37.666
- All the time.
- We'll just see.

221
00:13:38.133 --> 00:13:41.200
- Ready, Ash? Let's do our best.
- Right, and we're gonna win.

222
00:13:41.666 --> 00:13:44.333
With so many people here, I'm battling twerps?

223
00:13:44.400 --> 00:13:45.733
Do it right or else.

224
00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:47.333
-Wobbuffet.

225
00:13:47.400 --> 00:13:48.933
All right, then.

226
00:13:49.000 --> 00:13:49.966
Battle begin.

227
00:13:54.400 --> 00:13:56.366
- Eevee, ready to go?
- Eevee!

228
00:13:56.433 --> 00:13:59.133
Pikachu, use quick attack on Slurpuff.

229
00:14:03.866 --> 00:14:05.700
Slurpuff, energy ball. Now.

230
00:14:06.966 --> 00:14:09.766
- Pika!
- Eevee, swift, let's go.

231
00:14:09.833 --> 00:14:10.966
Eevee!

232
00:14:13.700 --> 00:14:14.900
Not too bad.

233
00:14:14.966 --> 00:14:17.366
Inkay, use psybeam on Pikachu.

234
00:14:20.800 --> 00:14:23.166
Pikachu, dodge and use iron tail now.

235
00:14:28.833 --> 00:14:30.833
No, Inkay!

236
00:14:30.900 --> 00:14:32.700
- What did I say?
- "Or else."

237
00:14:33.333 --> 00:14:35.733
- Pi! Pika, Pika!
- Eevee!

238
00:14:35.800 --> 00:14:39.600
Great job. Eevee doesn't look bothered by the attention anymore.

239
00:14:39.666 --> 00:14:41.833
- Mm-hm.
- All right. Keep it up.

240
00:14:41.900 --> 00:14:42.833
Eevee.

241
00:14:43.266 --> 00:14:44.700
No surprise. They're good.

242
00:14:45.166 --> 00:14:46.900
Well, I've got an idea.

243
00:14:46.966 --> 00:14:49.333
- Will you help me out?
- Yes, of course.

244
00:14:49.400 --> 00:14:51.033
First off, attack.

245
00:14:51.100 --> 00:14:52.733
Inkay, psybeam, let's go.

246
00:14:53.700 --> 00:14:54.900
Dodge it.

247
00:14:55.700 --> 00:14:57.466
Use cotton spore.

248
00:15:02.666 --> 00:15:04.100
One more time. Now.

249
00:15:04.166 --> 00:15:05.900
Inkay, psybeam, again.

250
00:15:11.566 --> 00:15:13.266
- Pikachu!
- Eevee!

251
00:15:13.333 --> 00:15:14.200
Pika...

252
00:15:14.633 --> 00:15:15.866
Inkay, tackle.

253
00:15:17.166 --> 00:15:19.166
That's what I call get-up-and-go.

254
00:15:20.266 --> 00:15:22.633
- Pika, Pika! Pika!
- Eevee!

255
00:15:23.600 --> 00:15:24.433
Pikachu, no.

256
00:15:24.933 --> 00:15:26.966
Eevee!

257
00:15:27.033 --> 00:15:29.066
Great. Finale time.

258
00:15:29.133 --> 00:15:29.966
Slurpuff.

259
00:15:31.533 --> 00:15:33.933
- Eevee!
- Yeah, you're right.

260
00:15:34.000 --> 00:15:36.366
Okay, now it's our turn.

261
00:15:36.833 --> 00:15:40.266
- Eevee, use swift.
- Eevee!

262
00:15:40.700 --> 00:15:44.066
- Use energy ball.
- Slurpuff!

263
00:15:47.533 --> 00:15:49.333
Inkay, use psybeam. Now.

264
00:15:50.100 --> 00:15:52.833
- Inkay!
- Eevee!

265
00:15:54.900 --> 00:15:56.833
- Eevee!
- Pikachu, can you still battle?

266
00:15:58.800 --> 00:16:00.433
- Pika.
- Yeah.

267
00:16:00.500 --> 00:16:02.500
Pikachu, use electro ball.

268
00:16:05.866 --> 00:16:07.733
Eevee, are you okay?

269
00:16:09.833 --> 00:16:12.000
- Thunderbolt, let's go.
- Use energy ball.

270
00:16:16.400 --> 00:16:19.666
I've never really been able to do anything at times like these.

271
00:16:20.400 --> 00:16:23.366
But somebody once told me my smile had the power

272
00:16:23.433 --> 00:16:24.933
to give others strength.

273
00:16:26.466 --> 00:16:29.666
Now I don't know how much strength I can give you, but...

274
00:16:30.333 --> 00:16:32.266
I wanna be your strength.

275
00:16:32.333 --> 00:16:33.533
Eevee.

276
00:16:37.100 --> 00:16:38.266
Huh?

277
00:16:43.966 --> 00:16:45.966
- What's going on?
- Is that...?

278
00:16:48.300 --> 00:16:49.533
It's evolving.

279
00:16:56.333 --> 00:16:58.700
- Sylveon.
- A Sylveon.

280
00:17:02.033 --> 00:17:04.233
Sylveon, the Intertwining Pokémon.

281
00:17:04.700 --> 00:17:07.166
Sylveon affectionately wraps its ribbon-like feelers

282
00:17:07.233 --> 00:17:09.566
around its trainer's arm, as they walk together.

283
00:17:09.633 --> 00:17:12.000
-Wow, Sylveon.

284
00:17:13.533 --> 00:17:15.633
You were right. We're not done.

285
00:17:15.700 --> 00:17:17.966
- The battle's not over yet.
- Yonny.

286
00:17:18.033 --> 00:17:19.233
Serena?

287
00:17:19.766 --> 00:17:21.533
Thanks for covering me, Ash.

288
00:17:22.033 --> 00:17:24.200
- You, too, Pikachu.
- Pika.

289
00:17:24.266 --> 00:17:26.466
It might have evolved, but I'm gonna win.

290
00:17:26.533 --> 00:17:28.700
Slurpuff, use energy ball.

291
00:17:30.900 --> 00:17:32.300
Dodge it, quick.

292
00:17:36.200 --> 00:17:37.233
It used fairy wind.

293
00:17:37.700 --> 00:17:40.133
- Wow, a new move.
- That's great, Sylveon.

294
00:17:40.600 --> 00:17:42.100
- Pikachu.
- Yon.

295
00:17:42.533 --> 00:17:44.766
Oh, dear. Here we go.

296
00:17:44.833 --> 00:17:46.766
Inkay, use tackle.

297
00:17:55.033 --> 00:17:56.933
It's true. It dances great.

298
00:17:57.033 --> 00:17:58.133
Yon.

299
00:17:58.766 --> 00:18:00.566
Now use fairy wind.

300
00:18:03.366 --> 00:18:04.566
Dodge it.

301
00:18:08.600 --> 00:18:10.133
- Slurpuff!
- Inkay, no!

302
00:18:11.700 --> 00:18:14.466
Slurpuff and Inkay are unable to battle,

303
00:18:14.533 --> 00:18:17.166
which means the winner is the team of Ash and Serena.

304
00:18:17.233 --> 00:18:19.400
S'il vous plaît, everybody,

305
00:18:19.466 --> 00:18:23.366
please give a big round of applause to mademoiselle and her partner.

306
00:18:23.833 --> 00:18:26.066
An exciting battle, indeed.

307
00:18:28.333 --> 00:18:30.500
- You guys were amazing.
- Yeah.

308
00:18:30.966 --> 00:18:31.900
Thanks a lot.

309
00:18:31.966 --> 00:18:33.500
Congratulations.

310
00:18:33.566 --> 00:18:35.233
You were great, Sylveon.

311
00:18:35.300 --> 00:18:36.633
- Pancham.
- Braixen.

312
00:18:39.600 --> 00:18:41.633
Wow, what a surprising evolution.

313
00:18:42.166 --> 00:18:45.000
- Huh?
- Eevee can evolve in many different ways.

314
00:18:45.066 --> 00:18:47.400
But it has to be especially close to its trainer

315
00:18:47.466 --> 00:18:49.300
to evolve into a Sylveon.

316
00:18:49.700 --> 00:18:50.866
I didn't know.

317
00:18:50.933 --> 00:18:52.666
Huh? Yonny.

318
00:18:53.300 --> 00:18:54.333
Hi there.

319
00:18:54.400 --> 00:18:55.633
You're beautiful.

320
00:18:56.100 --> 00:18:57.366
What is wrong with you?

321
00:18:57.433 --> 00:18:58.800
Sorry about that.

322
00:18:58.866 --> 00:19:01.466
- Inkay.
- Wobbuffet.

323
00:19:01.533 --> 00:19:02.800
Oh, well. That's life.

324
00:19:03.266 --> 00:19:04.766
And life makes me hungry.

325
00:19:06.033 --> 00:19:08.466
To thank you all for your attendance today,

326
00:19:08.533 --> 00:19:12.266
I will let you in on where the next Pokémon Showcase will be held.

327
00:19:12.333 --> 00:19:16.233
And that exciting location is... Fleurrh City.

328
00:19:16.300 --> 00:19:17.500
- Serena?
- Huh?

329
00:19:17.566 --> 00:19:20.500
We'll settle this at the next Showcase.

330
00:19:21.133 --> 00:19:22.566
Hmm. Yeah.

331
00:19:24.633 --> 00:19:28.466
Amazing. That girl and her Sylveon were wonderful together.

332
00:19:28.900 --> 00:19:31.966
How unusual of you to speak so highly of someone.

333
00:19:32.433 --> 00:19:37.000
Maybe. But I'm sure you'd feel exactly the same way if you'd seen them.

334
00:19:37.066 --> 00:19:38.600
They were dazzling.

335
00:19:38.666 --> 00:19:39.833
Right? Don't you think?

336
00:19:39.933 --> 00:19:41.400
Delph.

337
00:19:41.466 --> 00:19:44.133
- I found someone, too.
- Huh?

338
00:19:44.200 --> 00:19:45.133
You did?

339
00:19:45.200 --> 00:19:49.166
It's still too early to know for sure exactly how she'll turn out.

340
00:19:49.233 --> 00:19:51.266
But she's like you once were.

341
00:19:51.333 --> 00:19:53.100
Huh. What do you mean?

342
00:19:54.133 --> 00:19:56.100
- Excuse me. It's time to go.
- Huh?

343
00:19:56.533 --> 00:19:57.600
Right away.

344
00:19:57.666 --> 00:19:58.966
Sorry, Palermo.

345
00:19:59.033 --> 00:20:00.566
I'll call you again soon.

346
00:20:00.633 --> 00:20:02.666
Take care. Do your best.

347
00:20:03.666 --> 00:20:06.566
Hmm. We need to work hard, too.

348
00:20:16.400 --> 00:20:19.766
- She's wonderful, isn't she?
- Yon, yon.

349
00:20:20.766 --> 00:20:24.133
- Sylveon, I'm happy we're a team.
- Yon, yon.

350
00:20:24.933 --> 00:20:26.866
Hey, Serena. Hurry up.

351
00:20:27.733 --> 00:20:28.566
I'm coming.

352
00:20:30.533 --> 00:20:33.433
So many amazing things have taken place.

353
00:20:33.533 --> 00:20:38.300
An unexpected reunion with a rival, and Eevee's evolution into Sylveon.

354
00:20:39.133 --> 00:20:42.800
Serena and her Pokémon are growing closer and closer.

355
00:20:42.866 --> 00:20:46.600
She's taken another big step forward as a Pokémon performer,

356
00:20:46.666 --> 00:20:49.533
as our heroes' journey continues.
